# M11.8 — a form's boxes, derived from the spec before the code existed.
#
# The UA sheet makes every control an atomic inline (M9.11) with one cell of
# horizontal padding either side — the cells a terminal draws a control's frame
# in, outside the content box, so `size` still buys the cells the page asked
# for. `body, p, form { margin: 0 }` takes the vertical rhythm out of the
# arithmetic; everything below is the control rules alone.
#
# `<p>before</p>`  — row 0.
#
# `<form>` — row 1. Three inputs, one box:
#   `size="17"` is 17 characters and a character is a cell, so the content box
#   is 17 wide and 1 row tall. Its margin box is 17 + 2 = 19. The newline
#   between `<form>` and `<input>` is a leading space on the line and is
#   dropped, so the margin box starts at x=0 and the content box at x=1.
#   `type=hidden` and `type=checkbox` generate no box at all: hidden because
#   HTML says so, checkbox because this engine recognizes the type and has not
#   implemented it (M11.12), and an empty text box would be a worse lie than
#   nothing.
#
# `<p>` with a `<textarea>` and a `<button>` — rows 2-4.
#   The textarea is `cols=20` × `rows=3`: content 20 × 3, margin box 22 × 3.
#   Its value is its text content with **one** leading newline stripped
#   (HTML §4.10.11) and every other space kept — "hello\ntextarea", two rows of
#   a three-row box. It is a value, not prose: no text box is generated for it
#   and it never reaches the paragraph's own line.
#   The button's label is its text content, so its content box is 6 × 1 and its
#   margin box 8; nothing separates the two elements in the source, so it
#   starts at x=22 and its content at x=23.
#   The line is 3 rows: a control's baseline is the row its own text sits on
#   (the last one), so the textarea contributes 2 rows above the baseline and
#   the button 0 — 2 + 1 + 0 = 3, baseline on row 4. The textarea therefore
#   fills rows 2-4 and the button sits on row 4.
#
# `<p>` with `width: 40px` — row 5. CSS wins over the attribute, as it does in
#   a browser: 40px is 5 cells, so `size=17` decides nothing here.
#
# `<p>after</p>` — row 6. The page is 7 rows.
<html>  x=0 y=0 w=40 h=7
  <body>  x=0 y=0 w=40 h=7
    <p>  x=0 y=0 w=40 h=1
      anonymous  x=0 y=0 w=40 h=1
        line  x=0 y=0 w=40 h=1
          #text "before"  x=0 y=0 w=6 h=1
    <form>  x=0 y=1 w=40 h=1
      anonymous  x=0 y=1 w=40 h=1
        line  x=0 y=1 w=40 h=1
          <input …> field value "typed"  x=1 y=1 w=17 h=1
    <p>  x=0 y=2 w=40 h=3
      anonymous  x=0 y=2 w=40 h=3
        line  x=0 y=2 w=40 h=3
          <textarea …> field value "hello textarea"  x=1 y=2 w=20 h=3
          <button> field label "Search"  x=23 y=4 w=6 h=1
    <p>  x=0 y=5 w=40 h=1
      anonymous  x=0 y=5 w=40 h=1
        line  x=0 y=5 w=40 h=1
          <input …> field value ""  x=1 y=5 w=5 h=1
    <p>  x=0 y=6 w=40 h=1
      anonymous  x=0 y=6 w=40 h=1
        line  x=0 y=6 w=40 h=1
          #text "after"  x=0 y=6 w=5 h=1
